Opened Command Prompt and verified Docker and Docker Compose versions.



Created a folder named jenkins-static-site on the E: drive.



Navigated to the project directory.



Created the docker-compose.yml file using Notepad.



Configured the Jenkins image, container name, port mappings, restart policy and persistent Docker volume.



Started Jenkins using the docker compose up -d command.



Verified that the Jenkins container was running using docker ps.



Retrieved the initial administrator password using the Docker exec command.



Opened http://localhost:8080 in the browser and unlocked Jenkins.



Installed the suggested Jenkins plugins and created an administrator account.



Opened Manage Jenkins → Plugins and installed the HTML Publisher plugin.



Created a new Pipeline job named karunya-site-pipeline.



Selected Pipeline script under the Pipeline definition.



Entered the pipeline script to generate the Karunya University website using HTML and CSS.



Configured the Generate site stage to create site/index.html and site/assets/style.css.



Configured the Publish site stage using the HTML Publisher plugin.



Added the archiveArtifacts step to archive the generated website files.



Saved the pipeline configuration and clicked Build Now.



Verified that the pipeline build completed successfully.



Opened Karunya University - Simple Site from the job page and confirmed that the website was displayed correctly.



Opened the successful build and verified that index.html and style.css artifacts were archived.
